with gives us some pricing power.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/05/04/hyatt-hotels-h-q1-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"H 2018 Q1","e":"h","d":"2018-05-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Analyst","x":"And if it is, do you think you have the flexibility now to go into deals with a partner and potentially streamline the process?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/05/04/hyatt-hotels-h-q1-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"H 2018 Q1","e":"h","d":"2018-05-03","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Patrick Grismer","x":"In our press release dated February 22, we increased our guidance on minimum shareholder capital returns for 2018 to at least $500 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/05/04/hyatt-hotels-h-q1-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"H 2018 Q1","e":"h","d":"2018-05-03","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Patrick Grismer","x":"As Mark and I mentioned this morning, we are very pleased with our better-than-expected results for the quarter and with an improved pace of group bookings in the quarter, we are confidently increasing our outlook in a few key areas.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/05/04/hyatt-hotels-h-q1-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"H 2018 Q2","e":"h","d":"2018-08-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Patrick Grismer","x":"And then finally, as a reminder, we took some fairly significant severance and other charges in the fourth quarter of last year, we'll be lapping that this year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/08/06/hyatt-hotels-h-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"H 2018 Q2","e":"h","d":"2018-08-01","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Patrick Grismer","x":"After another quarter of strong operating results, solid momentum in group bookings and greater visibility to the remainder of the year, we are increasing our outlook for growth in both RevPAR and adjusted EBITDA.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/08/06/hyatt-hotels-h-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"H 2018 Q2","e":"h","d":"2018-08-01","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Patrick Grismer","x":"With respect to adjusted EBITDA, we are raising our full-year guidance to a range of $775 million to $785 million, effectively lifting the low end of the range by $10 million and the midpoint by $5 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/08/06/hyatt-hotels-h-q2-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"H 2018 Q3","e":"h","d":"2018-10-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Patrick Grismer","x":"The first would be reorganization costs, which would encompass both severance and relocation associated with the restructuring of the organization as we integrate it into Hyatt.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/31/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q3-2018-earnings-conference-ca.aspx"},{"c":"H 2018 Q3","e":"h","d":"2018-10-31","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Patrick Grismer","x":"Finally, we are reducing our guidance for full-year capital expenditures to approximately $325 million, reflecting a shift of certain costs into 2019, which we expect will show higher levels of spending, given the number and nature of projects under way at that time.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/31/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q3-2018-earnings-conference-ca.aspx"},{"c":"H 2019 Q2","e":"h","d":"2019-08-01","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Mark S. Hoplamazian","x":"Separately, I want to briefly comment on our reduced guidance for adjusted EBITDA which Joan will cover in more detail.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/01/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcri.aspx"},{"c":"H 2020 Q2","e":"h","d":"2020-08-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joan Bottarini","x":"Cost savings associated with those reductions compared to our original plan translate into about 35% reduction in our monthly SG&A and approximately 40% reduction in our monthly costs for certain systemwide services that are reimbursed by our hotel owners.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcri.aspx"},{"c":"H 2020 Q2","e":"h","d":"2020-08-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joan Bottarini","x":"During the second quarter, we utilized approximately $20 million less cash per month than the $90 million monthly burn rate we originally assumed excluding severance payments and other onetime costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcri.aspx"},{"c":"H 2020 Q3","e":"h","d":"2020-11-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joan Bottarini","x":"Our cost savings measures and operational efficiencies have pushed breakeven level down to the bottom of those ranges.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/06/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcri/"},{"c":"H 2020 Q3","e":"h","d":"2020-11-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joan Bottarini","x":"During the third quarter, our monthly cash burn, excluding severance payments and other onetime costs, decreased from our second quarter cash burn.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/06/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcri/"},{"c":"H 2020 Q4","e":"h","d":"2021-02-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark S. Hoplamazian","x":"We took the difficult but necessary steps to reduce headcount and discretionary costs, resulting in an over $100 million reduction in SG&A expenses, excluding bad debt expenses as compared with our original 2020 guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/18/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcri/"},{"c":"H 2020 Q4","e":"h","d":"2021-02-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joan Bottarini","x":"During the fourth quarter, our monthly cash utilization, excluding severance payments and other onetime costs, was slightly better than our previously provided second half 2020 expectations, ranging from $60 million to $65 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/18/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcri/"},{"c":"H 2021 Q1","e":"h","d":"2021-05-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joan Bottarini","x":"During the first quarter, our average monthly cash utilization, excluding severance payments and other onetime costs, materially improved to $42 million per month versus an expectation of $55 million to $60 million per month based on Q4 demand levels.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/05/hyatt-hotels-corp-h-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcri/"},{"c":"H 2025 Q4","e":"h","d":"2026-02-12","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mark Hoplamazian","x":"In addition to that, the government is taking action to facilitate getting building products brought in without undue tariffs and taxes and labor.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/12/hyatt-hotels-h-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"H 2025 Q4","e":"h","d":"2026-02-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joan Bottarini","x":"If you look at the contribution of Playa and the impact of the restructuring of the credit card earnings into our co-brand earnings into our results, we end up with a midpoint of core fee growth that is exceptionally strong.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/12/hyatt-hotels-h-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"H 2026 Q1","e":"h","d":"2026-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mark Hoplamazian","x":"We are very sensitive to what is happening with airfares because airlines will have to adjust their fares to accommodate fuel price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/30/hyatt-h-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"H 2026 Q2","e":"h","d":"2026-07-30","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Joan Bottarini","x":"We reaffirmed our guidance with respect to capital returns for this year between $325 million and $375 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/07/30/hyatt-h-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"H 2026 Q3","e":"h","d":"2026-10-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Joan Bottarini","x":"Finally, we are raising our full year outlook for capital returns to shareholders to between $375 million and $425 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/31/hyatt-h-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[33,1,8954,0,0,0,7636,942],[34,1,7786,0,0,0,6532,827],[35,1,10035,0,0,0,8224,1366],[37,1,10388,0,0,0,8993,976],[38,1,9591,0,0,0,8193,971],[39,1,8747,0,0,0,7673,773],[40,1,9802,0,0,0,8409,950],[41,1,9089,0,0,0,7714,1034],[42,1,8522,0,0,0,7372,838],[43,1,9217,0,0,0,8035,864],[44,1,9865,0,0,0,8931,688],[45,1,8550,0,0,0,7609,637],[46,1,8586,0,0,0,7570,657],[47,1,8189,0,0,0,7230,679],[64,1,9016,0,0,0,6247,947],[65,1,6630,0,0,0,5390,823],[66,1,8919,0,0,0,7364,1104],[67,1,8467,0,0,0,6982,1207]],"cinema":[[33,1,8954,0,0,0,7636,942],[34,1,7786,0,0,0,6532,827],[35,1,10035,0,0,0,8224,1366],[37,1,10388,0,0,0,8993,976],[38,1,9591,0,0,0,8193,971],[39,1,8747,0,0,0,7673,773],[40,1,9802,0,0,0,8409,950],[41,1,9089,0,0,0,7714,1034],[42,1,8522,0,0,0,7372,838],[43,1,9217,0,0,0,8035,864],[44,1,9865,0,0,0,8931,688],[45,1,8550,0,0,0,7609,637],[46,1,8586,0,0,0,7570,657],[47,1,8189,0,0,0,7230,679],[64,1,9016,0,0,0,6247,947],[65,1,6630,0,0,0,5390,823],[66,1,8919,0,0,0,7364,1104],[67,1,8467,0,0,0,6982,1207]],"imax":[[33,1,8954,0,0,0,7636,942],[34,1,7786,0,0,0,6532,827],[35,1,10035,0,0,0,8224,1366],[37,1,10388,0,0,0,8993,976],[38,1,9591,0,0,0,8193,971],[39,1,8747,0,0,0,7673,773],[40,1,9802,0,0,0,8409,950],[41,1,9089,0,0,0,7714,1034],[42,1,8522,0,0,0,7372,838],[43,1,9217,0,0,0,8035,864],[44,1,9865,0,0,0,8931,688],[45,1,8550,0,0,0,7609,637]